I've played some fairly old versions (ones which ran great on a 512k
PC-XT with twin 360k drives), but I'm not sure if they were quite as
old as yours.  The following spoilers relate to many versions prior
to version 3.0.



















Aside from the normal things you probably need to survive (armor,
weapons, food, ...), the following were needed:
   - fire resistance (ring, or intrinsic)
   - some way to level teleport (I believe that in some early
     versions, the only way to do this was to read a scroll
     of teleportation while confused) to the level with the amulet.

   - Although not strictly necessary, a ring of teleport control
     makes it much easier to get to the correct level.

Sometimes you just couldn't find everything you needed.  Instead of
hiding a wand of wishing in the castle (like version 3.0 or later),
in the original hack, a wand of wishing was in the lowest level you
could reach with the stairs.  It was hidden under a boulder pushed
up against a dead end on level 25 or so.  To get it, you needed to
either dig the wall away and push the boulder, or drop everything
you owned, and try to squeeze into the boulder square.  If you didn't
have anything to dig with, I think even in the ealiest version there
was a minotaur who carried a wand of digging.

So the basic sequence to win is:
  - develop an incredible character
  - Walk down as deep as you can, and get the WOW from the boulder
    (there are no scrolls of charging, so I think you only get 3
     wishes - I don't know about squeezing out a forth).
  - Wish for the remaining things you need.
  - Level teleport to the lowest level (I think level 30).
  - All the levels from 25-30 (approx) only have up stairs.  Make
    your way from level 30 up until you find the wizard.  Kill him,
    take the Amulet, and walk up (and up and up...).

Things I'm not sure about:
  - Was there a wizard in the very earliest version, or was the Amulet
    just sitting on level 30?  Under a boulder or something?
  - Was the wizard always on level 30 (25?) in some versions?
  - I think in some versions all the maze levels without downstairs
    had a wand of wishing under a boulder.  As I recall a potion of
    object detection showed the "/" not the "'", so you may want to
    use a potion of object detection, note all the "/", and wander to
    each one.
  - The wizard may be in a room with no entrance, surrounded by water.
    You may need to push a boulder into the water, and use your wand of
    digging to open the room (I'm not sure in which version this was
    introduced)


